    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d565">

                <pb facs="0786" n="772" xml:id="pg772"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.93/1762: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-04-11T09:00:00+07:00">April 11, 1944—9
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:01 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>631. Consul [at] Tihwa reports in telegram April 6 following information obtained
                    from Foreign Affairs Delegate (Embassy’s 613, April 6):</p>
                <p>Six hundred Kazaks attacked Sinkiang caravan during night April 4 at point south
                    of Fuwen located 60 kilometers this side of Mongol-Soviet border.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
